 "narrative": [
  "Bachelor of Science in Education Sciences: Transforming Education through Research and Practice.",
  "Students must meet the following requirements: one lower-division course (at least two units) and a total of eleven upper-division courses (at least fifty units), with a minimum of six courses within the Department of Education Studies.",
  "To satisfy the requirements for the major, lower- and upper-division courses must be completed with a P, C–, or better grade.",
  "Except for independent study course electives (EDS 197, 198, or 199) which are always taken with a Pass/No Pass grade option, students may take up to two courses, either lower or upper division, with a Pass/No Pass option.",
  "All students in the Education Sciences major are required to complete fieldwork hours in an educational setting.",
  "Students in the major have the option of completing a specialization in Elementary Educational Practices; Secondary Educational Practices; and Educational Research and Outreach (no separate requirements listed).",
  "Students who plan on applying to the graduate program to obtain a California Single Subject Teaching Credential must complete a second major in the content area of their planned teaching credential."
 ]
}